  "details": "As stated in the recent devlog:\n\n\"What about filters so I can completely turn off this content?\"\n\n\"We’re not adding them. Filters get set once and forgotten, and then you never see that part of VRChat again. In addition, a filter assumes that labels are correct, so it inherits all the problems we talked about above. This all results in world discovery and community issues that we’re not keen on having.\"\n\nThis brings up a really interesting point, content filters are disabled by default for new and often younger users who are typically unaware such a feature exists to begin with, and if one of these users happened to accidentally enable such a filter they would miss out on so many parts of VRChat without ever knowing! This could all be easily rectified so all users can get equal and fair exposure to all content including: \n\nSexually suggestive \n\nAdult language and themes\n\nGraphic violence\n\nExcessive gore\n\nExtreme horror\n\nIt only makes sense to really make sure every user regardless of preference or age gets to see every bit of VRChat! Please consider fixing this oversight as soon as possible!",
